  "instructions": [
    "Heat a large pan over medium heat. Add the lamb shoulder and sear until browned on all sides. Remove the lamb and set aside. Add the onion, carrot, and celery to the pan and cook until the vegetables are tender. Add the garlic and cook for 1 minute. Add the hot sauce and cook for 1 minute. Add the flour and cook for 1 minute. Add the ale and bring to a boil. Return the lamb to the pan and cover with a lid. Simmer for 2 hours. Mix the beurre monte and add to the stew. Season with thyme, salt, and pepper. Serve hot."
